/id "q-94485" :question/id #uuid "2e9f175e-8026-51c8-a30f-c784766388ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-94485" :question/problem "Given the elliptic cone $\\frac{(x-6)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{8}=\\frac{(z+6)^{2}}{6},$ find its intercepts with the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To find the $y$-intercepts of the elliptic cone, we plug $x=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0-6)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{8} & =\\frac{(0+6)^{2}}{6} \\\\ \\frac{36}{9}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{8} & =\\frac{36}{6} \\\\ 4+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{8} & =6 \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{8} & =2 \\\\ (y-4)^{2} & =16 \\\\ y-4 & =\\pm 4 \\\\ y & =4\\pm 4 \\\\ y & =0,8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $y$-axis are $(0,0,0)$ and $(0,8,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94485/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e0b4012-403b-5739-8f33-3c79111129fd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94485"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94490/selection/ed43e33d96833b8eb36aa11008d7a7998731afba14a5385eade843e2557f680e" :answer/id #uuid "fc590fb5-d7a0-5705-936f-881aef7fc854" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$z=-x,\\,$ $z=x+2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94490/selection/7d902fccc798f8fe25db741bd8e716a2e493065f67f5683069a8b0fe0038cf73" :answer/id #uuid "20bc7cb0-2d31-5c85-aceb-46ef1a12734e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$z=-x-2,\\,$ $z=-x$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94490/selection/20e8bc22a54a1043a4304f22c51f5994ff14fb7fe77e92cfc1ef26cfdfc499e3" :answer/id #uuid "7d58e0fe-29b2-5231-94df-da48ec6ac6c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94490/selection/0a330f976d8d5f993ffd6253c3d3123c7ca8e0155c3a1ceec59550f4cfd58141" :answer/id #uuid "98ad9488-f0f3-59f3-a6fe-5837e8a90116" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\pm x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94490/selection/85d774879bceb87ee75d1ebce90228242be8c0e6fc0a1b6ea81275af2a4ab7b3" :answer/id #uuid "ad600997-cab7-59fb-a5bb-6ece9ab1b40b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\pm x-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94490/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b2cbb472-de5f-5adf-a705-50a67dfcb947" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94490/selection/ed43e33d96833b8eb36aa11008d7a7998731afba14a5385eade843e2557f680e" :answer-field/choices ["q-94490/selection/ed43e33d96833b8eb36aa11008d7a7998731afba14a5385eade843e2557f680e" "q-94490/selection/7d902fccc798f8fe25db741bd8e716a2e493065f67f5683069a8b0fe0038cf73" "q-94490/selection/20e8bc22a54a1043a4304f22c51f5994ff14fb7fe77e92cfc1ef26cfdfc499e3" "q-94490/selection/0a330f976d8d5f993ffd6253c3d3123c7ca8e0155c3a1ceec59550f4cfd58141" "q-94490/selection/85d774879bceb87ee75d1ebce90228242be8c0e6fc0a1b6ea81275af2a4ab7b3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94490" :question/id #uuid "4d859ee6-f828-506d-b2a6-7efbe3346f4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-94490" :question/problem "What is the trace in the $xz$-plane of the elliptic cone $(x+1)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}=(z-1)^{2}\\,?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2}+\\frac{{0}^{2}}{6} & =(z-1)^{2} \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =(z-1)^{2} \\\\ \\pm (x+1) & =z-1 \\\\ z & =\\pm (x+1)+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two lines in the $xz$-plane with equations $z=-x$ and $z=x+2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94490/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb7148a2-58cc-5023-845c-435b47e31c83"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94490"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94605/selection/9fd2cb0d8b05ff91706261a62c6496a73b74fb8b6dc7a0d202fba22d3c5b283b" :answer/id