ion/problem "Given the elliptic cone $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}={z}^{2},$ find its intercept with the $z$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To find the $z$-intercept of the elliptic cone, we plug $x=0$ and $y=0$ into the equation and solve for $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{0}^{2}}{9} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ 0+0 & ={z}^{2} \\\\ {z}^{2} & =0 \\\\ z & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intercept with the $z$-axis is $(0,0,0)$ only." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94605/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e0b4012-403b-5739-8f33-3c79111129fd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94605"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94698/selection/f2499705abcb2c89174f0c4acc973d74573290008beb8091b859e00163b1e2d4" :answer/id #uuid "f74cb226-6321-5bab-b031-b5d47abbda2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4,9,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94698/selection/b69160273df5837b20faeaa082a3ff3045b66b3d7a16c83006518331475b7f00" :answer/id #uuid "9eab0653-fbac-5a84-a3c4-cb16e5c433d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-3,-2,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94698/selection/3815aeb1780c26fc80fb65bfe8fae09070ac21d98177c79fa356448b34eb33ed" :answer/id #uuid "7bf00957-4239-53b5-a587-5f4c553ebaf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-9,-4,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94698/selection/a64fffc5b0dcc946debc701d7c83324abb3c90a1ea26e389f5b3d261be7b0183" :answer/id #uuid "def33a8a-7ed1-521d-8ef8-d3d7153aedb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(9,4,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94698/selection/166a4f89fd3c58fa8af327fae523b712a1b6cfdcf88aad43a346572d0eaa9a53" :answer/id #uuid "6caf5be3-72ab-5114-9ce8-5796b324e988" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3,2,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94698/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "44ee014d-2d30-51a5-a5f4-af0e289c22f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94698/selection/b69160273df5837b20faeaa082a3ff3045b66b3d7a16c83006518331475b7f00" :answer-field/choices ["q-94698/selection/f2499705abcb2c89174f0c4acc973d74573290008beb8091b859e00163b1e2d4" "q-94698/selection/b69160273df5837b20faeaa082a3ff3045b66b3d7a16c83006518331475b7f00" "q-94698/selection/3815aeb1780c26fc80fb65bfe8fae09070ac21d98177c79fa356448b34eb33ed" "q-94698/selection/a64fffc5b0dcc946debc701d7c83324abb3c90a1ea26e389f5b3d261be7b0183" "q-94698/selection/166a4f89fd3c58fa8af327fae523b712a1b6cfdcf88aad43a346572d0eaa9a53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94698" :question/id #uuid "bcc2e3e3-89bb-5607-9c6a-ce5e59ebb032" :question/math-academy-id "q-94698" :question/problem "Find the center of the elliptic cone $9(x+3)^{2}+4(y+2)^{2}={z}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of an elliptic cone with center at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-{x}_{0})^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-{y}_{0})^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=\\frac{(z-{z}_{0})^{2}}{{c}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTo find the center, we rewrite our equation in standard form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9(x+3)^{2}+4(y+2)^{2} & =(z-0)^{2} \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{1/9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{1/4} & =(z-0)^{2} \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-3))^{2}}{1/9}+\\frac{(y-(-2))^{2}}{1/4} & =(z-0)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of an elliptic cone that has its center at $(-3,-2,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94698/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e0b4012-403b-5739-8f33-3c79111129fd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94698"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-176835/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "ad076e91-5f00-51fe-8611-2b87707fb879" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-176835/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "cefba145-4076-5b1a-aaf4-c6cc40a50274" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-176835/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "0b320a2e-92d8-52d4-b617-2a8f70b0421e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-176835/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "d0416f8b-a1ef-546a-9011-ccdc83b6c7ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-176835/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "a604bc03-6712-5fa8-888d-872bf83b126e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-176835/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d225e5c8-4d5a-5189-b8b6-41c036c699a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-176835/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-176835/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-176835/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-176835/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" "q-176835/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-176835/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-176835" :question/id #uuid "b96d3db6-3bd4-5dd7-9484-9554529374d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-176835" :question/problem "Given that the intersection of the elliptic cone $4(x+3)^{2}+8(y-1)^{2}=(z+7)^{2}$ and the plane $z=-3$ is an ellipse, what is the length of its major axis?" :question/worked-solution "To find the intersection of the elliptic cone and the plane $z=-3,$ we substitute $z=-3$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x+3)^{2}+8(y-1)^{2} & =(-3+7)^{2} \\\\ 4(x+3)^{2}+8(y-1)^{2} & ={4}^{2} \\\\ 4(x+3)^{2}+8(y-1)^{2} & =16 \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{(2)^{2}}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of an ellipse with a semi-major axis of length $a=2.$ Therefore, the major axis has length $2a=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-176835/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb7148a2-58cc-5023-845c-435b47e31c83"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-176835"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
